CORE gcc-only gcc16 libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 5 --no-unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ size: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ value found again: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ count: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of (?!system-header function '(operator(\*|/|<<|>>)=|operator\(|lexicographical_compare_three_way))
--
Was KNOWNBUG with the headers of libstdc++ 16 (gcc 16) only (silent wrong
result: assertions 2 and 3 FAILURE without any front-end diagnostic).  Fixed by
round 160/161: `__builtin_clzg', `<=>' on pointers (strong_ordering), and the
static-member-template-of-a-base / braced-init / constexpr-array fixes that
made <compare>'s comparison-category helpers type-check.  Runs where the host
gcc is >= 16 (tag libstdcxx16).
The compound-assignment and conversion operators of <bits/max_size_type.h>
(unsigned __int128 arithmetic, named by the ranges machinery but not called
here) and
lexicographical_compare_three_way (map's operator<=>, `auto __cmp = __comp(...)'
with __comp's return type not yet deduced) are still dropped; the forbidden
pattern excludes exactly those.
